Let's do the Role + RoleBinding demo using YAML files. We'll grant monitoring-sa permission to read Pods in the default namespace only.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

How it works

                                                ServiceAccount: monitoring-sa  
                                                              ⬇
                                                RoleBinding: pod-reader-ns-binding
                                                Connects the identity to the Role
                                                              ⬇
                                                        Role: pod-reader-ns
                                              Allows get, list and watch on Pods in 

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Step 1 — Create the Role

apiVersion: rbac.authorization.k8s.io/v1
kind: Role
metadata:
  name: pod-reader-ns
  namespace: default
rules:
  - apiGroups: [""]
    resources: ["pods"]
    verbs: ["get", "list", "watch"]


# kubectl apply -f pod-reader-role-ns.yaml
role.rbac.authorization.k8s.io/pod-reader-ns created

# kubectl get role pod-reader-ns -n default
NAME            CREATED AT
pod-reader-ns   2026-10-13T17:50:32Z

- What this means: The Role defines read-only Pod permissions in the default namespace.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Step 2 — Create the RoleBinding


apiVersion: rbac.authorization.k8s.io/v1
kind: RoleBinding
metadata:
  name: pod-reader-ns-binding
  namespace: default
subjects:
  - kind: ServiceAccount
    name: monitoring-sa
    namespace: default
roleRef:
  apiGroup: rbac.authorization.k8s.io
  kind: Role
  name: pod-reader-ns


# kubectl apply -f pod-reader-rolebinding-ns.yaml
rolebinding.rbac.authorization.k8s.io/pod-reader-ns-binding created


# kubectl get rolebinding pod-reader-ns-binding -n default                                                                                           
NAME                    ROLE                 AGE
pod-reader-ns-binding   Role/pod-reader-ns   39s


Remember:
  - subjects identifies who receives the permissions.
  - roleRef identifies the Role whose permissions are granted.
  - The RoleBinding's namespace determines where those permissions apply.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Step 3 — Test the permissions

i) Check whether monitoring-sa can list Pods in default:
# kubectl auth can-i list pods \                                                                                                                      
  -n default \
  --as=system:serviceaccount:default:monitoring-sa
yes


ii) Now check kube-system:
# kubectl auth can-i list pods \                                                                                                                     
  -n kube-system \
  --as=system:serviceaccount:default:monitoring-sa
no

Expected: no from this RoleBinding alone. Your earlier ClusterRoleBinding still exists and grants monitoring-sa permission to list Pods across namespaces,
so with both bindings active, the actual result will be yes.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Final comparison
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
                                                                                                                       |
Feature                              Role + RoleBinding                      ClusterRole + ClusterRoleBinding          |
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|
Permission scope                      One namespace                          Cluster-wide when bound cluster-wide      |
Can grant Pod read access                  Yes                                              Yes                        |
Can grant Node access                 Not through a namespaced Role                         Yes                        |
YAML resource types                    Role, RoleBinding                       ClusterRole, ClusterRoleBinding         |
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|
